      "body": "## Summary\n\nRejects `enable_lora=True` at model initialization for Jamba with a descriptive `ValueError` before launching worker initialization or profiling forward passes.\n\n## Motivation & Context\nJamba (`JambaForCausalLM`) is an SSM/hybrid architecture that does not implement `SupportsLoRA`, nor does it have LoRA adapter implementations for its Mamba/MoE projection layers. When `enable_lora=True` was passed, `JambaModel` previously accepted the configuration and forwarded `is_lora_enabled=True` to `MambaMixer`. During the worker profiling forward pass, unaligned/non-contiguous tensor operations in the unadapted Mamba mixer triggered a CUDA illegal memory access (`torch.AcceleratorError`) and a fatal process abort (`terminate called after throwing an instance of 'c10::AcceleratorError'`).\n\nThis patch checks `vllm_config.lora_config` at the start of `JambaModel.__init__` and raises `ValueError(\"enable_lora=True is not supported for Jamba.\")`, matching the explicit rejection pattern used in Mamba2 and Zamba2. Includes CPU-side unit test verification.\n\nFixes #61853\n",
      "changedFiles": 2,
      "comments": {
        "nodes": [
          {
