    {
      "body": "We need to rethink how we should support LoRA for this model, also cc @linitra24 ",
      "created_at": "2026-10-17T16:16:55Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/61915#issuecomment-6236471090",
      "id": 6236471090,
      "updated_at": "2026-10-17T16:16:55Z",
      "user": {
        "login": "jeejeelee"
      }
    },
    {
      "body": "Makes complete sense @jeejeelee. If the goal is full LoRA support on Jamba (adapting both the attention projections and Mamba SSM mixer blocks), that definitely warrants a dedicated architectural pass.\n\nIn the meantime, this PR acts as an immediate defensive guardrail to prevent the hard CUDA illegal memory access / fatal process crash (\\\terminate called after throwing an instance of 'c10::AcceleratorError'\\) reported in #61853, matching the explicit rejection pattern in Mamba2 and Zamba2 until full adapter support lands.\n\nHappy to adapt this or hold it in draft while you and @linitra24 evaluate the roadmap for Jamba LoRA!",
      "created_at": "2026-10-18T14:04:58Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/61915#issuecomment-6250843122",
      "id": 6250843122,
      "updated_at": "2026-10-18T14:04:58Z",
      "user": {
        "login": "patrickswedish"
      }
    },
    {
      "body": "> Makes complete sense @jeejeelee. If the goal is full LoRA support on Jamba (adapting both the attention projections and Mamba SSM mixer blocks), that definitely warrants a dedicated architectural pass.\r\n> \r\n> In the meantime, this PR acts as an immediate defensive guardrail to prevent the hard CUDA illegal memory access / fatal process crash (\\ erminate called after throwing an instance of 'c10::AcceleratorError') reported in #61853, matching the explicit rejection pattern in Mamba2 and Zamba2 until full adapter support lands.\r\n> \r\n> Happy to adapt this or hold it in draft while you and @linitra24 evaluate the roadmap for Jamba LoRA!\r\n\r\nSince the non-MoE parts of `JambaForCausalLM` can support LoRA, I don't think it makes sense to reject `enable_lora` outright. ",
      "created_at": "2026-10-18T14:10:07Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/61915#issuecomment-6250895311",
      "id": 6250895311,
      "updated_at": "2026-10-18T14:10:07Z",
